 No subjective audio quality or successful native transcription is asserted by
 these tests. Inspect recorded native callbacks/permission outcomes explicitly.
+
+## Chapter 8 workbench and accepted settings
+
+The existing `gui.Run` command still hosts terminal and WebSocket views of one
+Agent. Its working directory now contains `cr/settings.json`. Missing settings
+use dark theme, Read aloud enabled, speed 1, font 16 and the Agent's budget
+policy (zero means the named default of 200 batches). Invalid/unreadable saved
+settings fail startup rather than being silently discarded.
+
+`update_settings` carries a sparse `settings` object. Full `current_settings`
+(on subscribe) and `settings_changed` snapshots always include `theme`,
+`tts_enabled`, `tts_speed`, `font_size`, and `max_tool_rounds`, including false
+and zero. Shared wire/disk validation normalizes unknown themes to dark,
+clamps speed to 0.5–5 and font to 12–24, and clamps a negative GUI budget to zero.
+Bad types/JSON/null scalar values are errors. The hub serializes validation,
+replacement-file save/rename, runtime application and broadcast; failed writes
+leave the old accepted settings active and send only `settings_error`.
+This is not a power-loss durability guarantee.
+
+The public Agent `SetToolBatchLimit`/`ToolBatchLimit` methods own the next-turn
+policy; the setter rejects negatives. Each human turn captures its allowance
+once. Zero selects 200; positive N allows N batches, not N individual tool
+calls. `Config()` remains the immutable launch snapshot. Engine request
+ownership is unchanged. GUI preferences never enter core configuration.
+
+The sidebar has Agents/Settings tabs, keyboard/pointer-resizable dividers, and
+one recursively rendered Agent node. Chat and actions reuse the same rendering
+and queue pipeline with independent scroll following. Accepted settings—not
+unacknowledged local drafts—drive the controls, system/light/dark theme, text
+size, Read aloud and every new utterance. Fractional rates through 2 are used
+exactly; the requested 2–5 range maps monotonically to native 2–3. Extended
+rates are approximate, not a claim about native engine timing.
+
+Local checks (no browser or real provider):
+
+```sh
+go test ./...
+node test/queues.mjs
+node test/workbench.mjs
+go build -o /absolute/owned/ensemble-gui ./cmd
+python3 test/settings_process.py /absolute/owned/ensemble-gui /absolute/new-owned-run-dir
+```
+
+The process fixture uses a loopback streaming HTTP provider but real Agent,
+file tools, stdin, WebSocket and restart. It preserves logs under its new owned
+run directory. Node speech/DOM boundaries are inert recording fixtures, not
+native audio, visual layout, microphone or human-usability proof. Those require
+separate authorized browser/native exercises.
